WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.860
Well, AKA at Southern [University] helped to get us established at LSU, okay?

2
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:16.160
We had vine sisters from Southern that paired up with each one of us to help us through the process.

3
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.480
They were the ones that met with us and talked about how you formulated an organization and all that.

4
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.580
So we really have to give credit to Gamma Eta Omega’s chapter because they were the ones that helped to get us started.

5
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:35.620
We didn’t have rush but we would have . . . I know I remember us having a tea.

6
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.560
We all had white dresses and we met in the Union upstairs in one of those rooms.

7
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:46.480
My job as Dean of Pledges was to outline the activities that we would do.

8
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.600
I would plan the social calendar, or the civic calendar, as such.

9
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.300
We would do . . . I would get them involved in anything in reference to the Pan-Hellenic council,

10
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.040
like the game . . . the football game that’s denoted here.

11
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:06.620
When we got ready to have certain ceremonies that the sorority dictates, you know, I would see to it that they wore the proper attire.

12
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:12.020
I was like the person who was responsible for them . . . the leader who was responsible for them,

13
00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.800
but they also had their own sponsor.

14
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.780
We solicited girls, each one of us would sponsor somebody if we could.

15
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:26.140
But if we sponsored, that really placed an extra responsibility because you had to see to it that they did what they were supposed to do.

16
00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.920
Plus you had to see to it that they maintained those grades.

17
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:39.420
We would financially support Sickle Cell, you know, organizations like that, United Way.

18
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.220
We would financially support those kinds of things.

19
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:52.440
I remember us going to Hillhaven Rest Home several times, and I remember us doing the Muscular Dystrophy, you know, generating money for that.

20
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.400
I remember us helping out with . . . In fact,

21
00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.200
that’s one of the things that we did when [Kerry] Pourciau ran for SGA [Student Government Association] president [at LSU].

22
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.080
We passed out flyers for that.
